Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: libfprint-egis0576-tod
Source: https://github.com/PHILIPPDEV5396/libfprint-egis0576
Comment:
 This source package builds one file, extra-driver/egis0576.c and its
 supporting sources under extra-driver/egis0576/, as a libfprint TOD
 module. extra-driver/ and extra-integration/ are symlinks to ../../driver
 and ../../integration, dereferenced into real files by build-series.sh
 before the source package is built (see debian/rules and ../meson.build).
 That staging step follows the symlinks with cp -rL, so the SOURCE package
 dpkg-buildpackage -S produces, which is what a PPA publishes, carries the
 whole of driver/ byte-for-byte, not only the files ../meson.build compiles.
 The stanzas below cover every file under extra-driver/, whether or not the
 built binary package links it, and each Files stanza's own comment says
 which. The driver's provenance, including which parts are original work
 and which are reverse-engineered for interoperability, is documented in
 full in the project's top-level PROVENANCE.md; this file summarizes it,
 using the same categories packaging/debian/copyright uses.

# Fallback for anything not matched by a more specific stanza below. Listed
# first: lintian's dep5 checker expects a global wildcard stanza to be the
# first paragraph, and warns (globbing-patterns-out-of-order) if a more
# specific pattern appears before it instead of after.
Files: *
Copyright: PHILIPPDEV5396
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later

# PROVENANCE.md category 1: original work written from scratch for
# libfprint, licensed the same as the rest of the tree. egis_engine_cleanroom.c
# is staged into the source package by the same cp -rL as everything else
# under extra-driver/, even though ../meson.build does not compile it (the
# built libfprint-2-tod1-egis0576 binary links only the vendor matcher, see
# the category 2 stanza's comment below). Exception: egis0576_proto.c's
# EGIS_STEP_TABLE is a 16-entry table taken byte-exact from the vendor
# DLL's .rdata, and PROVENANCE.md places it in category 2 (see the Files
# stanza below); dep5 has no way to license part of a file separately, so
# this stanza covers the file as a whole and the exception is recorded
# here in prose, matching packaging/debian/copyright's treatment of it.
Files: extra-driver/egis0576.c
       extra-driver/egis0576.h
       extra-driver/egis0576/egis0576_proto.c
       extra-driver/egis0576/egis0576_proto.h
       extra-driver/egis0576/egis_rt.c
       extra-driver/egis0576/egis_rt.h
       extra-driver/egis0576/egis_engine.c
       extra-driver/egis0576/egis_engine.h
       extra-driver/egis0576/egis_engine_cleanroom.c
Copyright: PHILIPPDEV5396
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later

# PROVENANCE.md category 2: reverse-engineered from Egis Technology's
# proprietary Windows driver for interoperability. PROVENANCE.md, "Reverse-
# engineered for interoperability - no copyright claimed by the author",
# states the author claims no copyright over these files and that they are
# Egis Technology Inc.'s intellectual property; it does not state that Egis
# Technology Inc. licenses them, so no license grant is asserted here. This
# is the matcher flavour the built binary package actually links
# (../meson.build's egis0576_engine static library); see the next stanza for
# the clean-room alternative, which is staged into the source package but not
# compiled here.
Files: extra-driver/egis0576/egis_funcs.c
       extra-driver/egis0576/egis_coherence_map.c
       extra-driver/egis0576/egis_preprocess.c
       extra-driver/egis0576/egis_init.h
       extra-driver/egis0576/egis_blobs.h
       extra-driver/egis0576/egis_dat.h
       extra-driver/egis0576/egis_decls.h
       extra-driver/egis0576/egis_intrin.h
Copyright: Egis Technology Inc. (no copyright claimed by the
 libfprint-egis0576 author)
License: LicenseRef-Egis-reverse-engineered-interop

# PROVENANCE.md category 3: the clean-room correlation matcher, copied
# byte-for-byte with its own licence header intact from a third party.
# ../meson.build does not compile these files into the binary package (the
# binary links the vendor matcher above, the package's default), but the
# source package staged by build-series.sh's cp -rL carries them, since
# extra-driver/ is a faithful copy of the whole of driver/.
Files: extra-driver/egis0576/tsteppy/*
